From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seismic <noreply@seismic.systems>
Date: Thu, 12 Dec 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dma: Allow __GFP_COMP by clearing flag for encrypted DMA

When memory encryption (TDX/SEV) is active, DMA allocations with
__GFP_COMP (compound pages) are forbidden. Instead of failing with
a warning and returning NULL, automatically clear the flag and
continue with the allocation.

This fixes a deadlock where NVMe driver operations would fail during
boot when TDX is enabled, causing all block device operations to hang.

Signed-off-by: Seismic <noreply@seismic.systems>
---
 kernel/dma/direct.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/dma/direct.c b/kernel/dma/direct.c
index 000000000000..111111111111 100644
--- a/kernel/dma/direct.c
+++ b/kernel/dma/direct.c
@@ -175,8 +175,9 @@ void *dma_direct_alloc(struct device *dev, size_t size,
 	 * allocations via CMA need to be marked as compound.
 	 */
 	if (force_dma_unencrypted(dev) && (gfp & __GFP_COMP)) {
-		WARN_ON_ONCE(1);
-		return NULL;
+		/* Auto-clear __GFP_COMP for encrypted DMA instead of failing */
+		gfp &= ~__GFP_COMP;
+		pr_debug("DMA: Cleared __GFP_COMP flag for encrypted device %s\n", dev_name(dev));
 	}

 	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_DMA_DIRECT_REMAP) && !gfpflags_allow_blocking(gfp) &&
--
2.43.0
